                        "sense_id": "95ce117f-5346-3839-a6d3-bfd030006704",
                        "entry_id": "40b0c41a-45c0-321a-a77a-fe976cf02196",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Substance de protection des fibres nerveuses."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d13287e-0468-46bb-ae74-aba27a586fa4",
                                "sense_id": "95ce117f-5346-3839-a6d3-bfd030006704",
                                "text": "La leucodystrophie, comme de nombreuses autres maladies orphelines, provoque une dégénérescence de la myéline."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a61bfbe-f58d-45ca-861f-9d038cda6176",
                                "sense_id": "95ce117f-5346-3839-a6d3-bfd030006704",
                                "text": "[La sclérose en plaques] le mécanisme de cette maladie correspond dans tous les cas à une atteinte de la gaine de substance blanche qui entoure les fibres nerveuses du système nerveux central, il devient possible de décrire ces signes comme étant « une dissémination spatiale et temporelle de signes compatibles avec une atteinte de la myéline centrale ». — (Lionel Naccache, Le Nouvel Inconscient : Freud, le Christophe Colomb des neurosciences, Odile Jacob, 2009, page 431)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "723fa5d0-3faa-4a09-a81c-dc28672ab4fe",
                        "source_entry_id": "40b0c41a-45c0-321a-a77a-fe976cf02196",
                        "source_sense_id": "95ce117f-5346-3839-a6d3-bfd030006704",
                        "target_lang_word": "myelin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "myelin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36c9899a-0b4b-3911-9875-ceefa579063b",
                                        "entry_id": "64240b26-050d-38f3-b5be-d509ccd8ef5c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A white, fatty material, composed of lipids and lipoproteins, that surrounds the axons of nerves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fae1748-1e4e-4db4-b5c6-1a293f3649fc",
                                                "sense_id": "36c9899a-0b4b-3911-9875-ceefa579063b",
                                                "text": "As the result of prolonged action of water upon myelin, bird's-nests-cells are also said to be produced, and we are certain we have seen, as the result of such prolonged action of water, the appearances thus compared."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a54f255e-6b24-4dc3-90da-fbd8089b6330",
                                                "sense_id": "36c9899a-0b4b-3911-9875-ceefa579063b",
                                                "text": "This gene controls the production of an insulating sleeve that wraps around neurons. Known as myelin, it is crucial for long-range communication in the brain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
